Maven/npm integration

Configure the existing Maven build to:

1. Install or use the required Node/npm environment in a controlled, reproducible way.
2. Run the frontend dependency installation and production build.
3. Copy the generated frontend assets into the appropriate Spring Boot static-resource location.
4. Package the React UI together with the existing backend application.
5. Preserve the ability to run the frontend independently during development.

Use the existing Maven conventions and available plugins. Do not add unnecessary plugins or change Java/Spring Boot versions unless required and approved.

Ensure the build supports the organization’s npm registry, internal network restrictions, and lockfile-based reproducibility.

