- Posting restriction details.

Use correct currency formatting and handle missing values.

F. Disposition overview

Provide a disposition list and detail view using confirmed disposition types, statuses, reasons, and identifiers.

Do not invent approval, waiver, release, or rejection actions. Only implement state-changing operations if the existing backend explicitly supports them and authorization requirements are understood.

G. Activity feed

Display events only if reliable activity/event data exists.

- Distinguish actual backend events from simulated demo events.
- Show timestamps and relevant identifiers where available.
- Do not fabricate real-time activity or imply that mock events came from production.

